+// Note [K VNNI storage]
+// ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+// With TRON_K_VNNI (CMake option, default OFF; requires TRON_AMX_DISPATCH) the
+// K plane of every 128-dim head holds the VNNI pair-interleaved layout of
+// tron/kernels/k_vnni.hpp instead of one row per token; the bytes and the
+// page capacity are the same, only the order of the values changes. The gate
+// is k_vnni::layout_on<head_size>, a property of the storage geometry: every
+// reader and writer of a slot sees the same layout, whatever the query type
+// and whether AMX is available at run time. V is unchanged (its
+// pair-interleaved layout is already the AMX B operand).
+//
+// Why: the AMX QK kernel reads the VNNI plane directly as its B operand and
+// computes S = Q . K^T in the orientation the softmax wants (qk_vnni_128x4),
+// so the transposing store of the row-major kernel (Note [QK orientation] in
+// amx_attn_iface.hpp) disappears, and there is no second copy of K to keep
+// coherent (the K mirror design this replaces kept a row-major K and a VNNI
+// copy of it in a parallel arena).
+//
+// Consumers of a VNNI slot, and how each one changes:
+//   1. save_k (model.hpp) stores the token's row with page::set_k_row, which
+//      scatters the 64 dim pairs into the token's column (k_vnni::scatter_row,
+//      4 AVX-512 scatters). The row-major store was 4 64-byte stores; the
+//      scatter touches 64 cache lines of the 16 KiB plane, which prefill
+//      writes 64 tokens at a time and decode once per step per (layer, KV
+//      head);
+//   2. the dense AMX page path (self_attention.hpp) hands page::k_vnni_plane
+//      to qk_vnni_128x4;
+//   3. the software path for partial pages, the kill switch
+//      (TRON_AMX_DISABLE=1) and hosts without AMX use k_vnni::qk_group, an
+//      AVX-512 reader with one token per vector lane (no per-token gather,
+//      no horizontal reduction); the row-major dotter loop is compiled only
+//      for row-major slots;
+//   4. the FPGA staging path (gof::populate -> shuffle_k_entry) needs one
+//      row per token: page_info::k_head_fn materializes it with
+//      page::get_k_row into caller-owned scratch, as v_head_fn already does
+//      for V. The staging bytes and the HBM layout are unchanged;
+//   5. page copies (copy_storage_slot: append and defrag) copy a whole page
+//      as one memcpy when the range covers the page, and otherwise move token
+//      by token (get_k_row + set_k_row), because a token's position inside
+//      the page decides its column;
+//   6. the row view page::k() does not exist for VNNI slots (a token's values
+//      are not contiguous); the layout-agnostic set_k_row / get_k_row
+//      accessors exist for every slot.
+// The kill switch keeps the layout: with TRON_AMX_DISABLE=1 a TRON_K_VNNI
+// binary runs the AVX-512 VNNI reader, not the row-major dotter, so it is a
+// same-layout AMX-off arm, not a rollback to the row-major binary's numerics
+// (the fp32 add order of the two readers differs; see the numerics contract
+// in Note [AMX attention dispatch]).
+
